Error [E0119]: `identity` expects 1 type argument, got 2
  --> tests/ui/generic_call_type_arity.jet:3:21
    |
  3 | fn run() { value :: identity<Int, String>(1) }
    |                     ^^^^^^^^
 Why: A generic call must provide one type for every declared type parameter
 Fix: Write identity with 1 type argument
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0119

Error [E0112]: `identity` wants `T` for argument 1, but this is Int (a whole number)
  --> tests/ui/generic_call_type_arity.jet:3:43
    |
  3 | fn run() { value :: identity<Int, String>(1) }
    |                                           ^
 Why: Every argument must match its parameter's type
 Fix: Use `T` here
